Requirements: 7   with obligations: 7

[task-01] When the review needs an edit that makes a named plausible defect true, it
    asks for several candidate edits instead of one and uses the first candidate that
    passes the checks the review already applies to an edit. How many candidates it asks
    for is configurable. A candidate that fails a check is set aside and the next is
    tried, and when no candidate passes, the defect is handled the way a defect no edit
    could be built for is handled today.
    -> candidate-edit-makes-defect-true  [human_review/explicit]
       The review needs an edit that makes a named plausible defect true.
    -> several-candidate-edits  [functional/explicit]
       The review asks for several candidate edits instead of one.
    -> use-first-passing-candidate  [functional/explicit]
       The review uses the first candidate edit that passes the checks the review
       already applies to an edit.
    -> candidate-count-configurable  [docs_config/explicit]
       The number of candidates the review asks for is configurable.
    -> failed-candidate-set-aside  [functional/explicit]
       A candidate that fails a check is set aside and the next candidate is tried.
    -> next-is-tried  [functional/explicit]
       A failed candidate edit is set aside and the next candidate is tried.
    -> fallback-handling-matches-no-edit-defect  [functional/explicit]
       When no candidate passes, the defect is handled the same way a defect for which
       no edit could be built is handled today.

[task-02] The review also gains one further check on whether an edit changes anything at
    all. The code is compiled before and after the edit and the two compiled forms are
    compared, so an edit that leaves behaviour untouched is refused even when its text
    differs from the text it replaced. A condition that is always true, a value the
    caller ignores, and a reordering with no effect each read as a change to the text
    and as no change to the compiled form, and each is refused here.
    -> compiled-form-change-check  [functional/explicit]
       The review compares the compiled forms before and after the edit to determine
       whether the edit changes anything at all.
    -> behavior-unchanged-edits-refused  [regression/explicit]
       Refuse edits that leave behaviour untouched, even when the edited text differs
       from the text it replaced.
    -> always-true-condition-is-refused  [regression/explicit]
       An edit that changes only a condition that is always true is refused because it
       leaves the compiled form unchanged.
    -> value-the-caller-ignores  [functional/explicit]
       The edit changes a value the caller ignores.
    -> no-effect-reordering-refused  [regression/explicit]
       A reordering with no effect is treated as a change to the text and as no change
       to the compiled form, so it is refused.
    -> no-op-change-refused  [regression/explicit]
       The change is refused when it leaves behavior untouched even if its text differs
       from the text it replaced.
    -> always-true-condition-refused  [regression/explicit]
       The change is refused when it introduces a condition that is always true.
    -> ignored-value-refused  [regression/explicit]
       The change is refused when it introduces a value the caller ignores.
    -> no-effect-reordering-refused-2  [regression/explicit]
       The change is refused when it only reorders code with no effect.

[task-03] For each defect, the review records how many candidates it asked for, how many
    it set aside and why, and which candidate it used. Its report says what building
    edits cost and how long it took, since asking for several candidates multiplies
    both.
    -> record-candidate-request-count  [functional/explicit]
       For each defect, the review records how many candidates it asked for.
    -> set-aside-count-and-reasons  [functional/explicit]
       Record how many candidates were set aside and why.
    -> which-candidate-it-used  [functional/explicit]
       Record which candidate it used for each defect review.
    -> report-captures-edit-cost-and-duration  [explanation_observability/explicit]
       The report states what building edits cost and how long they took.

[constraint-01] Two runs over the same input pick the same candidate.
    -> deterministic-candidate-selection  [invariant/explicit]
       Two runs over the same input pick the same candidate.

[exclusion-01] Whether an edit that passes the checks really makes its named defect
    true.
    -> defect-truth-not-judged  [functional/explicit]
       The review does not assess whether an edit that passes the checks really makes
       its named defect true.

[exclusion-02] Which plausible defects are enumerated, and which region of the code an
    edit is allowed to fall in.
    -> exclude-defect-enumeration-and-edit-region  [functional/explicit]
       The change does not alter which plausible defects are enumerated, and it does not
       alter which region of the code an edit is allowed to fall in.

[exclusion-03] Running the candidate tests, and anything decided from what they did.
    -> no-candidate-test-execution-decision  [regression/explicit]
       The change does not include running the candidate tests or making any decision
       based on their results.

